<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Na Atabia</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1700</span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Na Atabia was a ruler (nayiri) of Mamprugu, the oldest of the Mossi-Dagomba kingdoms in northern Ghana, around 1700. Under him the royal capital moved from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gambaga">Gambaga</a> to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nalerigu">Nalerigu</a>, which remains the seat of the Mamprugu king, while Gambaga continued as a centre for Muslim traders and scholars linking the kingdom to Hausaland and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/akan">Akan</a> forest.</p></div>
